      "updated": 1744740737773,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Forbidden?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Forbidden?",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "7Y485clS9aHHHTylmYBZU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 336.34928995374673,
      "y": -114.07626136968435,
      "width": 949.7078947574297,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bER",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1602508468,
      "version": 2439,
      "versionNonce": 104531852,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1744741249760,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Check if forbidden:\n1. Lets try to find a valid total ordering for writes based on coherence:\n    x: 0 -> 1\n2. For y, we know that R[y]* = 1 is program-ordered before R[y] = 3.\n2. For the lwsync from Thread 1, it only requires the following:\n    For any particular thread, W[x] = 1 to propagate to that thread before W[y] = 1\n3. The sync from Thread 3 only requires:\n    W[x] is committed and propagated to other threads before R[x] starts.\n\nBelow is a possible ordering:\n1. Thread 1 finished W[x] = 1 and W[y] = 1.\n2. Thread 2 performs R[y]* = 1 and W[y]* = 2.\n3. Thread 3 performs W[y] = 3 and performs a sync.\n4. Thread 2 performs R[y] = 3.\n5. Since there is no requirement that W[y] = 1 has propagated to Thread 3, W[x] = 1\nneed not propagate to Thread 3, allowing R[x] = 0 to happen.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Check if forbidden:\n1. Lets try to find a valid total ordering for writes based on coherence:\n    x: 0 -> 1\n2. For y, we know that R[y]* = 1 is program-ordered before R[y] = 3.\n2. For the lwsync from Thread 1, it only requires the following:\n    For any particular thread, W[x] = 1 to propagate to that thread before W[y] = 1\n3. The sync from Thread 3 only requires:\n    W[x] is committed and propagated to other threads before R[x] starts.\n\nBelow is a possible ordering:\n1. Thread 1 finished W[x] = 1 and W[y] = 1.\n2. Thread 2 performs R[y]* = 1 and W[y]* = 2.\n3. Thread 3 performs W[y] = 3 and performs a sync.\n4. Thread 2 performs R[y] = 3.\n5. Since there is no requirement that W[y] = 1 has propagated to Thread 3, W[x] = 1 need not propagate to Thread 3, allowing R[x] = 0 to happen.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
